2-
3-> **Status: DRAFT by the owner instance (Claude Opus 5.5), revised after the Codex non-author review
4-> (`docs/reviews/amendment-11/CODEX-REVIEW.md`, A11-01 to A11-07; `DISPOSITION.md`). Not signed.** The author's
5-> first commit containing the final text is its signing act. Layered on the original and Amendments 1–10, none of
6:> which is edited. Every registered sentence this amendment changes is listed in §A11.3.
7->
8-> **Outcomes informed this amendment** (the original's amendment rule). Each change is disclosed separately.
9:> - **§A11.2, P3.** The P3 evidence (`formal/p3-verification-profile/`) was built and reviewed before this text.
10->   Building it exposed the stale checklist. No P3 result failed and is relabelled here. The floor's shape is the
11->   author's proposal of 2026-10-28.
12-> - **§A11.5 item 2, the slot-2 boundary.** This is a **retrospective relaxation** of a deadline-qualified
13->   restriction. It is proposed after the 21 Oct deadline, and after the candidate code (`service/signer-gcp/`) was
14->   written and reviewed.
15-> - **§A11.5 item 5, K-R's enforcement.** The owner's placement decision (2026-10-27) moved KMS signing from the
16->   issuer role to a dedicated policy signer and said it changed no registered sentence. It changed the
17->   supplement's description of who computes μ and who may sign. The confirmation review found this.
18-> - **§A11.5 item 3, the spike keys.** The owner's deployment draft had contradicted a registered commitment. That
19->   draft is withdrawn, and this amendment changes nothing in the commitment.
